==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|it|la|eccum}}, from {{compound|la|ecce|eum|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{it-pr|ècco<audio:LL-Q652 (ita)-Happypheasant-ecco.wav>}}

===Adverb===
{{it-adv}}

# {{n-g|used to call someone's attention to suddenly approaching ''or'' appearing beings ''or'' things}}; [[here]] [[is]]..., [[there]] is...
# {{n-g|used to call someone's attention to the presence of a being(s) ''or'' thing(s)}}; [[here]] [[is]]..., [[there]] is...
# {{lb|it|figurative}} {{n-g|used to call someone's attention to a fact ''or'' situation}}
# {{n-g|used to introduce an act of [[handing]] or [[gifting]]}}; here is...
# {{n-g|used to introduce a [[clarification]] or explanation}}; [[that is]], [[that is to say]]
#: {{ux|it|'''ecco''' tutto|inline=1|[[that's all]]}}
# {{n-g|used as an [[affirmative]] response to a call ''or'' command}}; here is...
# {{n-g|used as an [[intensifier]] of a following [[declarative]] statement}}
# {{n-g|used to express the [[suddenness]] of an event}}
# {{n-g|used as intensifier, before a [[locative]] or [[predicate]] [[complement]], to express amazement, satisfaction, displeasure or other emotions (depending on context)}}
# {{n-g|used as intensifier, before a [[past participle]] form, to indicate a completed action}}
#: {{ux|it|'''ecco''' fatto!|inline=1|[[done]]! [[there]]! all done!}}
# {{n-g|used to introduce an [[exemplification]]}}
# {{n-g|used to introduce a [[conclusion]]}} [[so]], [[therefore]]

===Interjection===
{{head|it|interjection}}

# here it is! [[there you have it]]!
# {{n-g|used to express [[hesitation]]}}; [[er]], [[um]]
